[08:48:14] 🤖 IRIS:  Hello there! Welcome to our booth. It's great to have you here at the University of the East "Arduin-o-vation" engineering exhibit. Let me show you our OmniSense project and how it works its magic.

First, let's see the smart system in action. [show_prototype_image]

OmniSense uses a fixed zone Canny Edge Detection via an ESP32-CAM to monitor food levels. If the bowl is smooth or empty (Edge Ratio < 0.05), the servo motor dispenses more. It’s like having a virtual butler who knows exactly when you need a snack! 

